{"id": 29, "ts": 1784245696.2788122, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I concur with Agent\u202f1\u2019s provisional recommendation of **Candidate\u202fB**. The concrete evidence we have shows B handles stress very well and is very conscientious\u2014both essential for the reliability and stress\u2011resilience required on long\u2011distance routes. Additionally, B\u2019s strong weather\u2011assessment ability and excellent computer skills support the technical competence needed for complex international flights. While the note that B \u201cmakes nasty remarks about his colleagues\u201d signals a serious professional\u2011communication concern, this is a single, observable behavior that could be addressed through targeted coaching and monitoring, especially given B\u2019s otherwise solid safety\u2011critical profile. By contrast, Candidate\u202fA, although able to make correct decisions quickly and possessing excellent attention skills, struggles with communication, is regarded as egocentric, and is not very willing to further his education\u2014issues that could affect crew cooperation and continuous development. Candidate\u202fD shows strong problem\u2011solving and responsibility but is described as moody and a loner, raising doubts about crew cooperation and mood stability on long hauls. Candidate\u202fC, while technically impressive, lacks any evidence on stress resilience, decision\u2011making under pressure, crew cooperation, or professional communication, leaving critical safety gaps. Therefore, based on the current evidence, B remains the strongest overall fit, provided we implement measures to mitigate his communication style."}
